gui.rfgen.tablet.arrow=>

gui.rfgen.tablet.p0.title=Fragment I — Discovery
gui.rfgen.tablet.p0.l1=[Translation] Looks like some ancient civilization built this.
gui.rfgen.tablet.p0.l2=Technology that makes use of wormholes — not magic, but geometry folded thin.

gui.rfgen.tablet.p1.title=Fragment II — The Builders
gui.rfgen.tablet.p1.l1=[Translation] They did not dig stars. They synthesized them.
gui.rfgen.tablet.p1.l2=Stone, quartz, and volcanic glass became a vein that never was.
gui.rfgen.tablet.p1.l3=What falls from that vein is unstable until fire teaches it order.

gui.rfgen.tablet.p2.title=Fragment III — Matter
gui.rfgen.tablet.p2.l1=Matter path (craft the ore, mine it, then refine):
gui.rfgen.tablet.p2.l2=Synthetic Ore -> Raw Naquadah (25%) -> Refined Naquadah (explode the raw item).

gui.rfgen.tablet.p3.title=Fragment IV — Power
gui.rfgen.tablet.p3.l1=Power path — each step borrows more of the wormhole:
gui.rfgen.tablet.p3.l2=Naquadah Generator (brief) -> Unstable Converter (longer) -> Wormhole Energy Converter (steady).

gui.rfgen.tablet.p4.title=Fragment V — Echoes
gui.rfgen.tablet.p4.l1=Duplication path — an item is remembered across a throat of space:
gui.rfgen.tablet.p4.l2=Wormhole Duplicator (reusable) / Unstable Duplicator (once, then collapse).

gui.rfgen.tablet.p5.title=Fragment VI — The Ground Remembers
gui.rfgen.tablet.p5.l1=Mineral Tuners persuade a chunk what vein it "always" had.
gui.rfgen.tablet.p5.l2=Requires Immersive Engineering excavator minerals. Consumed on success.

gui.rfgen.tablet.p6.title=Fragment VII — Closing
gui.rfgen.tablet.p6.l1=[Translation] Do not ask the wormhole for diamonds made of diamonds.
gui.rfgen.tablet.p6.l2=For exact crafts and chances, consult JEI — this tablet only remembers the road.
